From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin <robinei@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:12:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/dsi: Frame start delay of 4 lines for DSI video mode
 on VLV/CHV

EXPERIMENT, not for upstream.

i915 always programs a frame start delay of 1 (TRANSCONF bits 28:27,
"reserved" in the public VLV PRM, but written by i915, the GOP and
Intel's Android driver). Intel's Android ADF DSI code computed the delay
for DSI pipes from an HW-team rule, (htotal * 5 ns * delay) >= 8000 ns,
max 4, which gives 4 for htotal 774. On a GPD Win 1 (CHV, DSI video
mode) the pipe intermittently stalls for one frame and the DSI stream
loses alignment; give the pipe more lead time at frame start to see
whether the pipe/DSI frame-start handshake is involved.

Note: the GOP leaves 1, so the boot takeover becomes a full modeset.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
index 877eab7..f175b5c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
@@ -280,6 +280,15 @@ static int intel_dsi_compute_config(struct intel_encoder *encoder,
 	pipe_config->sink_format = INTEL_OUTPUT_FORMAT_RGB;
 	pipe_config->output_format = INTEL_OUTPUT_FORMAT_RGB;
 
+	/*
+	 * EXPERIMENT: frame start delay of 4 lines for DSI video mode on
+	 * VLV/CHV, as Intel's Android driver computed for DSI pipes
+	 * ((htotal * 5 ns * delay) >= 8000 ns, max 4).
+	 */
+	if ((display->platform.valleyview || display->platform.cherryview) &&
+	    is_vid_mode(intel_dsi))
+		pipe_config->framestart_delay = 4;
+
 	ret = intel_panel_compute_config(intel_connector, adjusted_mode);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
